    "summary": "Epic Bird Song and unstoppable He's Gone>Truckin'>The Other One jam",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a soaring Bird Song and a marathon second‑set sequence that runs from He's Gone through Truckin' into The Other One without losing momentum. Jerry’s lead work, Keith’s jazzy keys and Phil’s “gold” bass solo keep the entire two‑hour trek tightly focused.",
    "review": "June 22, 1973 at Vancouver's P.N.E. Coliseum captures the band in a relaxed West‑Coast groove that blossoms into one of their most memorable second‑set marathons. The first set eases listeners through classics like Box of Rain and a beautifully rendered Bird Song before launching into a high‑energy stretch featuring Here Comes Sunshine, Black Peter and a jaw‑dropping Playing In The Band. The real fireworks ignite with He's Gone → Truckin' → The Other One, a seamless, jazz‑inflected journey that showcases Phil’s “gold” bass solo, Keith’s piano textures and Bill’s crisp drumming. The set closes on a jubilant Sugar Magnolia and a rousing encore of Casey Jones and Johnny B. Goode, making this night a quintessential snapshot of the 1973 era.",
